emma: Customer on Vercel edge seeing ReadableStream hang during streaming after token rotation. SSE stream returns a 401 mid-stream and the client read loop never exits. SDK v0.12.4. Can someone help repro and confirm if this is the same as the recent auth-retry issue? High priority for them.

ryan: Can you paste a minimal repro and what environment (node version / runtimes)? Also any logs from the client side.

emma: Repro steps. Short Node example (Edge runtime / Vercel):
```js
// edge streaming repro
const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.example/v1/chat/stream', {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` }
});
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  console.log('chunk', new TextDecoder().decode(value));
}
console.log('stream closed');
```
package.json excerpt:
```
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@redwood/inference": "0.12.4"
  }
}
```
Node 18.x on Vercel edge, customer sees: chunk x3, then no more logs, process stays alive. We instrumented network and saw server respond with 401 on an auth refresh endpoint while the SSE connection remained open. No close/end event on reader.

liz: I think this is the auth-retry + stream lifecycle bug we fixed recently. In 0.12.x the SDK tries to refresh tokens but doesn't properly abort the active ReadableStream when a 401 is encountered during incremental SSE chunks, so the `reader.read()` promise never resolves.

ryan: Can you paste the raw client-side console log snippet (timestamps okay)? Also did the customer use our built-in token rotation helper or roll their own?

emma: Logs: 
[13:02:01] chunk 1 (90 bytes)
[13:02:03] chunk 2 (120 bytes)
[13:02:05] chunk 3 (95 bytes)
[13:02:07] network: 401 returned for token refresh, suspect rotation happened
[13:02:07] no 'done' from reader, no further chunks, process still waiting on reader.read()
Customer used our client helper with ephemeral rotation callback.

liz: That matches. Workaround: add an AbortController with a timeout around fetch so reader.read() will be aborted on unexpected hangs. Example:
```js
const ac = new AbortController();
const t = setTimeout(() => ac.abort(), 20000);
const res = await fetch(url, { signal: ac.signal, headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` } });
clearTimeout(t);
// then read as normal
```
But that's a bandaid. The correct fix is in 0.13.1 where we ensure any 4xx during streaming triggers a stream abort and surfaces an error to the reader. Can you try upgrading to 0.13.1 (or our nightly) and repro?

emma: Customer can't upgrade immediately. Any small patch we can recommend?

liz: If they must stay on 0.12.x, we can suggest patching their local bundler to wrap the fetch response with a `ReadableStream` that times out on no-chunk period, or inject a small helper to detect no-progress and call `reader.cancel()`. Example detect-no-progress pattern:
```js
let last = Date.now();
const check = setInterval(() => {
  if (Date.now() - last > 15000) {
    reader.cancel().catch(() => {});
    clearInterval(check);
  }
}, 5000);
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  last = Date.now();
}
clearInterval(check);
```
It's ugly but buys time.

ryan: I'll open a backport patch to 0.12.x to forcibly cancel streams on auth failure. Creating PR runtime-stream-fix/3421 and will request a canary build.

deploy-bot: Canary build 0.13.1-rc.1 deployed to hosted stream cluster (edge) for testing.

ryan: Patch open: https://git.internal/redwood/runtime/pull/3421 — it force-aborts streams on 401 during SSE frames and adds test coverage for ReadableStream lifecycle.

emma: I gave the customer the workaround and they were able to detect and cancel the stream; they can test the patch tomorrow. Thanks.

liz: After patch lands, we'll also add a note to the streaming troubleshooting doc about token rotation and recommended abort timeouts.

emma: Great. Marking this as monitored for the customer. Will update if they confirm resolution. :thumbsup:

ryan: Follow-up: merged backport to release branch and cut 0.12.5 patch. QA will run edge regression suite tomorrow.

emma: Awesome — closing once customer verifies.
